<title>USA: McDonnell gets $1.267 bln for F-18 work.</title>
<headline>McDonnell gets $1.267 bln for F-18 work.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp is being awarded a $1.267 billion modification to a previously awarded contract to provide full funding for fiscal 1997 low-rate initial production of eight F-18E and four F-18F aircraft, the U.S. Navy said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The work, which will be performed in St. Louis, Missouri, and Hawthorne, California, is expected to be completed by April of 2000, the Navy said.</p>
